<title>CHINA: China bank in $65 million loans to Iran, Zimbabwe.</title>
<headline>China bank in $65 million loans to Iran, Zimbabwe.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Export-Import Bank of China has signed agreements to extend loans worth more than $65 million to Iran and Zimbabwe to finance purchase of machinery and equipment, the China Daily said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bank would loan $35 million to Zimbabwe Iron and Steel to buy equipment and technology from China's Capital Iron and Steel Corp for blast furnace renovation, it said.</p>
<p>Iran would receive a loan of $30.6 million to import X-ray facilities from China National Chemical Construction Corp, it said.</p>
</text>
